cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "A Scaling-Cancellation Principle for Chord-Based Geometric Approximations"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Baker
    given-names: C. Wayne
date-released: 2026-06-28
version: preprint-v1
repository-code: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/scaling-cancellation-principle"
url: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/scaling-cancellation-principle"
abstract: >-
  This note formulates a Richardson-type scaling-cancellation principle for
  chord-based geometric approximations with even-power asymptotic expansions.
  It proves that a two-scale combination cancels the leading inverse-square
  error and distinguishes fixed-resolution order improvement from the
  nonlinear cubic residual map of the Baker 4:3 trisection cascade.
keywords:
  - scaling cancellation
  - Richardson extrapolation
  - chord approximation
  - polygonal approximation
  - asymptotic analysis
  - geometric N-series
  - trisection cascade
license: proprietary
